  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="f224-4fdf-53b5-878b" name="Israelite (Chariot Wars) - List Notes" publicationId="513c-2d0a-024a-da5a" hidden="false">
      <description>ISRAELITE ARMY LIST (Chariot Wars, pp.47-52).
Characters up to 25%; at least one character to command. A small army of 1,000 points can be commanded by a Senior Officer rather than a General (or King). Chariotry &amp; Cavalry up to HALF the points value. Infantry at least 25%. Allies &amp; Mercenaries up to HALF.
Early armies (Joshua, Saul, David) were almost entirely infantry; later armies (Solomon onwards) have a strong chariot force. The Sacred Ark may only be chosen if the army has no chariots.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS:
[Israelite]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Chariotry &amp; Cavalry: up to 50%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 50%
  Standard composition.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
